<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boris I of Bulgaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 852–889; d. <a href="/years/907">907</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Saint Boris, Boris-Michael, Saint Boris I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boris I was ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a> from 852 to 889. He accepted Christian baptism around 864, taking the name Michael, and secured an autonomous Bulgarian church under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. In 886 he welcomed the disciples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyril-and-methodius">Cyril and Methodius</a>, whose schools at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/preslav">Preslav</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohrid">Ohrid</a> developed Slavonic literature. He retired to a monastery, briefly returning in 893 to depose his son Vladimir, and is venerated as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boris-i-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="Boris I of Bulgaria" width="250" height="342" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boris_I_of_Bulgaria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The early Bulgars worshipped the sky god Tangra, while the Slavs kept their own pagan cults, until <b>Boris I</b> accepted baptism from Byzantium in 864 and imposed Christianity on his people.</blockquote><a href="/empire/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>During the reigns of Presian and <b>Boris I</b> in the mid-9th century their territory passed to the First Bulgarian Empire, and the name disappears.</blockquote><a href="/state/berziti">Berziti</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliska">Pliska</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/preslav">Veliki Preslav</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.36,27.13&amp;year=879" aria-label="Pliska on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5203 625 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Boris I of Bulgaria"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5653 895h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5653 895h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=43.36,27.13&amp;year=879">What was here in 879 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
